WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:07.399
right now in almost two dozen states across
the country, Republicans who control state

00:00:07.399 --> 00:00:10.500
legislatures are working on legislation.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:17.410
We just saw one in Texas a couple of days
ago that would make it a felony to protest

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:23.179
an oil pipeline or a chemical plant or an
oil refinery or a refinery.

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:27.750
They want to make protesting any of these
so called infrastructure projects as they

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.080
call them a felony.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.710
Now, the law that just passed the house in
Texas, uh, originally it was going to make

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.380
it punishable by up to 20 years in prison.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.140
But they decided maybe that was a little too
harsh and they bumped it down to now if this

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:48.890
law passes, you're only gonna get 10 years
in prison for protesting the placement of

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:51.580
an oil pipeline.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:57.010
What's happening here is that they're trying
to argue that these protesters come along

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:06.579
and they interrupt economic activity or they
damage critical pieces of fossil fuel infrastructure.

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:11.030
Now I understand we don't like these pipelines
and I do not advocate damage to them of any

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.060
kind.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:18.790
However, a peaceful protest is allowed by
the constitution.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:22.380
Just because you don't like it doesn't mean
you can pass a law at the state level saying,

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.250
you can't do this.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.409
That's unconstitutional.

00:01:27.409 --> 00:01:32.280
We have the right to peaceably assemble here
in the United States.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:37.979
You cannot take that away just because you
want to keep flooding this country with fossil

00:01:37.979 --> 00:01:40.830
fuels and toxic chemicals.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.069
And yet that is exactly what these states
are working on.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.520
And let me go through some of the list here.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.520
I already mentioned Texas.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:51.189
Here we have Oklahoma individuals who protest
pipelines can now be smacked with a $100,000

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:52.729
fine and 10 years in prison.

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:57.719
This, according to the Sierra Club, Louisiana
says activists who make unauthorized entry

00:01:57.719 --> 00:02:04.240
of a critical infrastructure such as oil pipelines,
face a punishment of up to five years in prison

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.969
and a $1,000 fine.

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:10.780
North Dakota last March passed a law under
which interfering with pipeline construction

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:15.810
becomes a felony punishable by up to five
years in prison and a $10,000 fine.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:22.590
And groups conspiring with such protests could
be criminal criminally liable for 10 times

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:23.590
that amount.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.159
So $100,000 fine for anybody who conspires
with these protesters.

00:02:27.159 --> 00:02:33.680
You know, perhaps a nonprofit, an environmental
organization that sets up these protests.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.019
See, they're not just going after the protesters
themselves.

00:02:37.019 --> 00:02:43.129
They're working on ways written into these
laws to defund the organizations who help

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:47.470
organize these events and these protests.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:48.510
That's phase two.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:53.890
First you take away everybody's First Amendment
right saying you cannot come and protest this

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:54.890
pipeline.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:03:01.469
And the second is we're going to bankrupt
and punish the organizations who are helping

00:03:01.469 --> 00:03:05.810
people organize these protests.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.000
That's a double whammy at this point.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.150
There's even more here and it's, it's absolutely
discussing, uh, officials in South Dakota

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:16.930
are arguing that there are limits to free
speech when protest comes into conflict with

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.829
economic interests.

00:03:19.829 --> 00:03:23.740
I don't remember seeing that in the first
amendment of the U s constitution.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:29.790
I, I don't think it said that our right to
peacefully assemble is limited as long as

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:34.150
it does not, you know, interfere with economic
activities.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:38.760
Other than that you're good to go, but hey,
you do anything that might disrupt the flow

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:43.329
of commerce than no, suddenly you can't do
it.

00:03:43.329 --> 00:03:45.010
That's not in the constitution.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:50.569
And that's one of the reason why these laws
are likely to fail.

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:56.870
But again, this is not the first time we've
seen a slew of laws come into play.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:02.280
At the same time we saw shortly after Charlottesville,
Republican controlled legislature is we're

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.040
trying to make it illegal for people to protest.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.670
You tried to limit where they could or could
not gather.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.750
And this wasn't in response to the horrible
people in Charlottesville.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:17.650
This was in response to the people who were
protesting the bad people.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:22.800
All of this boils down to the fact that they
want to take away our constitutional rights.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.300
That's what every one of these laws is designed
to do.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.860
Otherwise, they wouldn't feel the need to
do it.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:31.860
Okay.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:35.380
But every one of these is likely to get struck
down in court.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:41.570
Even if it goes up to one of the most conservative
justices in this country, they understand

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:51.520
too, regardless of their ideology, that you
can not infringe on that particular, right,

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.590
because if you do, then what's going to happen
the next time somebody challenges the Second

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:58.270
Amendment right?

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.650
You know, and says, well, wait a minute.

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.770
You've already dismantled the first amendment.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:06.669
Why don't we start dismantling the second
one too that would actually save lives here

00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:08.740
in the United States?

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.180
I don't think that's ever going to happen,
but it's something that these conservatives

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:16.380
need to have in their back pocket so that
they understand that at all times you come

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.810
after the amendments that matter, then you're
going to see people coming after the only

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:24.300
amendment that you seem to care about.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:28.010
But nonetheless, we should all be upset about
this regardless of your ideology.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:35.639
They are trying to strip us of our constitutional
rights and that is not something that is ever

00:05:35.639 --> 00:05:38.470
okay in this country.

